{"overview":"A Polish family, left homeless in the wake of World War I, move to Germany and struggle to survive during the Great Inflation. War orphan Inga has only accumulated a small amount of money from the rubble and hopes to wed Paul. Weakened by poison gas, Paul begins to invest in Inga's future and serves as their symbol of optimism.","tagline":"A Simple Romance of Love and Potatoes","cast":[{"n":"Carol Dempster","c":"Inga","p":"/azSHQHijC9MLNw5e4HkA56PjgLY.jpg","q":"Q932255"},{"n":"Neil Hamilton","c":"Paul","p":"/23jm1XwaaBKWTp5fKs7kzThK4KZ.jpg","q":"Q922580"},{"n":"Erville Alderson","c":"The Professor","p":"/mlrduJuut47E82jiTsSw74LtY3i.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Helen Lowell","c":"The Grandmother","p":"/zKmzd4JUUn1BISsq1jDUGorM9MR.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Marcia Harris","c":"The Aunt","p":"/gQOMrnTDWqTTCKvXngWHsAHrefB.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Frank Puglia","c":"Theodor","p":"/r1wLNTEnjKEQGrfUB5qzf8RpiCn.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Lupino Lane","c":"Rudolph","p":"/wFroJOcJqZE8uQQMyaBSc1Zd9se.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Hans Adalbert Schlettow","c":"Leader of the Workers","p":"/vH9V40S4DsKceDEZiWgCZZabKky.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Paul Rehkopf","c":"Hungry Worker","p":"/8EVxQ1JfSCw0CrOujlFOa0HtPKe.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Robert Scholtz","c":"Hungry Worker","p":null,"q":null}],"country":["United States"],"language":["English"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isn%27t_Life_Wonderful","qid":"Q6085139","rel":{"US":{"d":"1924-12-05","c":"NR"}}}